WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.534
-Guys, can we talk about
"Ghostbusters?"

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:05.868
-"Ghost Spookers."
-"Ghost Spookers: Afterlife,"

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.734
or "Ghost Stoppers: Afterlife."
This is --

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.501
There's a connection
between this story

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:13.334
and the original "Ghostbusters."
-Everyone that has seen it

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:14.968
says that they cry at the movie,

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.834
so it should be an extremely
successful comedy.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.133
-No, there's some great new
creatures, great new fun in it.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:25.300
The Ecto is doing things
that you never saw it do before.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.767
McKenna Grace
is a spectacular actress,

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:31.133
and she's basically
gonna be our new CEO.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.567
-Yeah.
-And then, we have, of course,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.300
Paul Rudd, a master comedian,
probably.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:41.367
You know, as Billy was
the leading comic, you know,

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.801
leading man of his generation,

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:46.667
Paul is gonna be taking
that torch up, I think.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:50.300
-Bill, do you think that you
should be Sexiest Man Alive?

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.167
-Yeah, I just happened to notice
out of the corner of my eye

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.767
Paul'S --
-Yeah. I was --

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.434
-Paul's mom comes around
with this magazine.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.801
-I came in 103rd.
-Paul's mom comes around?

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.734
-Paul's mom has been walking
up and down the halls

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:03.300
with this magazine.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.100
-She bought all the copies?
She's very proud.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.033
She's a very proud mom, yeah.
-She's great.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.133
And Carrie's great.
Carrie Coon, she's great.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.901
Just a fantastic cast.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.534
-What's it like
to put the suit back on?

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.567
Did you ever think
you'd do it again?

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.868
-You know,
I never thought we would,

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.834
up until I got there
and I realized

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.234
it's actually happening.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.300
But I will say,
when I got in the suit

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.901
and Bill and Dan
and seeing Sigourney,

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:28.234
it was almost spiritual, man.
I was almost in tears.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.167
It was great.
-What was it like

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.801
putting the suit back on, Bill?
Did it go, well?

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.801
-It hurt.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:36.234
[ Laughter ]
Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:39.167
-It was a lot of pain.
And, you know, the nice thing

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.968
about working
with a classically trained guy

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.501
is that he helps you
back to your feet.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:45.400
-Wow, exactly right.
-For some reason, they just --

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.234
these directors just
like to say, "Okay, now you guys

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.801
are all down on the ground,"

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.167
you know,
with this thing on your back.

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.868
And then you got to roll over
like a dead bug

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:57.000
and try to get up while wearing
a, you know, a vacuum cleaner."

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.400
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.934
-But it was -- you had shock
waves of memory from it.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.300
You went, "Oh, God.
This is horrible."

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.234
'Cause it was really
very, very long days.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.767
And it was a very heavy thing.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.467
It's not as heavy as the
original was, but we're weaker,

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.734
so it's about the same.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.934
-You've actually become weaker,
of course.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.133
I'm so happy
that you're here on the show,

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.067
and I love you guys so much.
Thank you so much.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.167
-Thanks, Jimmy,
for having us on.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.467
-I want to show a clip.
Here's a peak

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.467
at "Ghostbusters: Afterlife."
Take a look at this.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:26.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.934
♪♪

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.934
[ Switch rattles ]

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.434
-[ Roars ]

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:52.534
-[ Screams ]
[ Glass shatters ]

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:54.300
-Yes!

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.434
-Uh...

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.501
We should probably
get out of here.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.300
-You're an adult.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.300
-Yeah.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.968
And liable.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.767
-You know what this means,
right?

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.968
Your grandfather
was a Ghostbuster.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:12.200
-Yeah, that's right!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.801
My thanks to the one and only

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:18.734
Bill Murray, Dan Aykroyd,
Ernie Hudson!

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:21.968
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife"
hits theaters this Friday.

